message.content:
{
  "window_id": "w0031",
  "observed_failures": [
    {
      "filename": "034.jpg",
      "field": "date",
      "predicted": "2018-08-09",
      "evidence_in_image": "Printed 'Date: 09/03/2018' (DD/MM/YYYY) near the Simplified Tax Invoice header",
      "nature": "Date parsed as MM/DD/YYYY instead of DD/MM/YYYY (Malaysian receipt convention)"
    },
    {
      "filename": "074.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "702.00",
      "evidence_in_image": "Receipt shows 'Subtotal: 102.00', 'Total Incl. of GST 102.00', 'Total Amt Rounded 102.00', 'Payment: 102.00' (GL Handicraft, safety pins 6 boxes x 17.00)",
      "nature": "OCR digit confusion 1<->7 on the leading digit of 102.00; a single-pass extraction accepted a misread value without cross-checking against the multiple other occurrences of the same number on the receipt"
    },
    {
      "filename": "077.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "23.26",
      "evidence_in_image": "Banh Mi CafE receipt shows the sequence 'Total (Inclusive of GST): 23.26', 'Rounding Adj: -0.01', 'TOTAL: 23.25'. The final, visually largest line is 'TOTAL: 23.25'.",
      "nature": "Picked an earlier intermediate 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' line instead of the final post-rounding 'TOTAL:' line; keyword selection prefers first match rather than final/bottom-most total"
    },
    {
      "filename": "078.jpg",
      "field": "total_amount",
      "predicted": "\"\" (empty string)",
      "evidence_in_image": "Thai Delicious Restaurant receipt clearly prints 'Total : 92.80' and 'Grand Total : 92.80' in a tabular layout",
      "nature": "(a) Extraction failed on this tabular layout where amounts live in a right-aligned column far from the 'Grand Total' label, and (b) the writer emitted an empty string instead of a real null, violating the strict-schema contract (task mandates null on failure)"
    },
    {
      "filename": "<overall>",
      "field": "task_reward",
      "predicted": "0.0 (binary) vs 0.909 field accuracy",
      "evidence_in_image": "n/a",
      "nature": "The verifier compares the Excel line-by-line; 4 cell mismatches force the binary reward to 0 even though per-field accuracy is high. Terminated at max_iterations (65) with no finish, so the final write may have been the last attempt without full self-verification."
    }
  ],
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "id": "RC1-date-format-ambiguity",
      "summary": "No explicit locale rule for DD/MM/YYYY-dominant Malaysian receipts; the ad-hoc dateutil-style parsing (or first-match pattern) can flip day/month when both are <=12.",
      "scope": "image-ocr skill — date extraction guidance is absent in original SKILL.md; candidate adds patterns but still only tries the first matching format and does not document that dmy must take precedence over mdy for this corpus."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC2-first-match-total-selection",
      "summary": "Total extraction uses first keyword hit within a tier. Receipts commonly show a sequence 'Total (Excl GST) -> Total (Incl GST) -> Rounding Adj -> TOTAL/Grand Total'; picking the first match returns an intermediate value.",
      "scope": "image-ocr skill — the candidate's extract_total iterates top-to-bottom and returns on the first match; it does not differentiate qualified vs final totals and does not add qualifier-based exclusions (EXCLUDING, INCLUSIVE OF, BEFORE ROUNDING)."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC3-single-pass-ocr-digit-confusion",
      "summary": "Single-variant OCR output is accepted as the source of truth for the amount. Common glyph confusions (1↔7, 0↔8, 5↔6, O↔0) corrupt digits like 102.00 -> 702.00. No cross-validation against other occurrences of the same figure on the receipt (subtotal/total/payment/change-back).",
      "scope": "image-ocr skill — multi_pass_ocr exists but concatenates text; it does not cast votes across variants, nor does it cross-check amount candidates against other numeric fields that typically agree (subtotal == total when GST already inclusive and discount==0)."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC4-tabular-layout-keyword-value-gap",
      "summary": "On tabular receipts (Thai Delicious, Perniagaan Zheng Hui) the amount is in a right-aligned column far from the label; OCR preserves them on the same line only with --psm 6/4. If the chosen PSM breaks the line, the keyword line has no number and the two-line fallback also fails because the next line is another label.",
      "scope": "image-ocr skill — the two-line fallback is too narrow; it should also look forward 1–2 lines for a token that looks like 'last number on the row anchored at the keyword's y-coordinate', and the skill should recommend image_to_data with block/line numbers to preserve row grouping on tabular layouts."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC5-null-vs-empty-string-writer-drift",
      "summary": "On extraction failure, an empty string was written into the Excel cell instead of a real Python None. The xlsx strict-schema skill mentions this but does not enforce a normalize-before-write step, and does not show a post-write re-read check that would catch '' or 'nan' cells.",
      "scope": "xlsx skill — the Canonical Pattern is correct in spirit but relies on the caller returning None; it should mandate an explicit sanitize step (replace '', 'None', 'nan', NaN -> None) immediately before to_excel, and extend the self-check to assert no cell is the string ''."
    },
    {
      "id": "RC6-no-finish-no-self-verification-at-max-iterations",
      "summary": "The source run hit max_iterations=65 and terminated without a finish; there is no evidence of a final re-read assertion loop on the produced Excel (dtype of total_amount strings, ordering, sheet name, null presence).",
      "scope": "xlsx skill (and image-ocr batch orchestration) — the skills do not require a terminal self-check that re-opens the output and asserts the strict-schema contract before claiming done."
    }
  ],
  "skill_defects": [
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Date extraction section is absent in the original and under-specified in the candidate: no explicit DD/MM/YYYY precedence rule, no handling of 2-digit years, no guidance to skip plausibly-wrong dates (e.g., future dates, printer-footer timestamps that duplicate the invoice date in a different format)."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "extract_total picks the first keyword hit within each priority tier. It does not prefer the LAST matching candidate within a tier, and it does not treat qualifier parentheticals ('Excluding GST', 'Inclusive of GST', 'Before Rounding', 'Rounded') as either exclusions or de-prioritizers."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Exclusion list is incomplete for this receipt family. Missing: 'ROUNDING', 'ROUNDED' (when used as a line label alone), 'SERVICE CHARGE' / 'SVC CHG', 'CASH', 'VISA', 'MASTERCARD', 'PAYMENT', 'CASH RECEIVED', 'POINTS', 'TAX AMT', 'EXC GST'. Several of these produced ambiguity in 063/064/087/088/097 and were only saved by other heuristics."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Multi-pass OCR output is a concatenated string, not a vote. There is no recommended consensus/majority mechanism across preprocessing variants and PSM modes, so a single bad pass can corrupt the final amount even when other passes read it correctly."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "No cross-field numeric sanity check. On most receipts, extracted total should equal one of: subtotal, cash tendered - change, sum of line items, or the amount printed next to CASH/VISA/MASTERCARD. The skill never leverages this redundancy to reject obvious OCR errors like 702.00 vs. four co-occurring 102.00 values."
    },
    {
      "skill": "image-ocr",
      "defect": "Tabular-layout extraction is unaddressed. For receipts where label and amount are on the same visual row but separated by whitespace columns, the skill should recommend using pytesseract.image_to_data and grouping tokens by (block_num, par_num, line_num) so the amount on the same row as 'GRAND TOTAL' is recoverable even when --psm 6 splits it."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "Strict-Schema section does not enforce a pre-write normalization step that coerces '', 'None', 'nan', NaN, and numeric-looking floats for string-typed columns into the correct representation. The example writes the dict directly; it should wrap each field in a small normalize() helper."
    },
    {
      "skill": "xlsx",
      "defect": "The Pitfalls checklist does not include an assertion recipe that opens the written file with openpyxl (not pandas) and checks that nullable cells are value=None (not ''), that string columns have cell.data_type == 's', and that the sheet set is exactly the one required."
    },
    {
      "skill": "cross-skill",
      "defect": "There is no shared 'stop condition' recipe: an end-of-pipeline self-check that re-reads the produced artifact and confirms the task contract, independent of the iteration budget. This leaves the run vulnerable to silent failure when max_iterations is reached mid-polish."
    }
  ],
  "repair_recommendations": [
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "Structured Field Extraction (Receipts / Forms) — Keyword Priority and Exclusions",
      "change": "Add an explicit 5-tier priority for totals and change the selection policy to 'last match wins within the highest non-empty tier': T1 GRAND TOTAL; T2 TOTAL ROUNDED / ROUNDED TOTAL / TOTAL AFTER ROUNDING / NETT? TOTAL; T3 TOTAL RM, TOTAL: RM, TOTAL AMOUNT, AMOUNT DUE, BALANCE DUE, TOTAL DUE; T4 standalone 'TOTAL' / 'AMOUNT' lines that are NOT followed by a qualifier parenthetical; T5 same but allowing qualifiers. Document that within T1–T4 the LAST matching line is chosen (receipts emit totals bottom-up).",
      "rationale": "Fixes 077.jpg-class errors where 'Total (Inclusive of GST)' precedes the final 'TOTAL:'; generalizes to any receipt with intermediate Total lines."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "Structured Field Extraction — Exclusion Keywords",
      "change": "Extend exclusions to: SUBTOTAL, SUB TOTAL, TAX, GST, SST, DISCOUNT, CHANGE, CASH TENDERED, ROUNDING, ROUNDING ADJ, SERVICE CHARGE, SVC CHG, PAYMENT, CASH RECEIVED, VISA, MASTERCARD, MASTER CARD, DEBIT, CREDIT, POINTS, LOYALTY, EXCL GST, EXCLUDING GST, INCLUSIVE OF GST (only when a later line of equal-or-higher priority exists). Note that INCLUSIVE OF GST should be demoted, not hard-excluded, because on some receipts it IS the final line.",
      "rationale": "Removes false positives seen on 077 and prevents similar issues on receipts where payment-method lines echo the amount."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "Structured Field Extraction — Date Extraction",
      "change": "State explicitly that for receipt-style corpora the DD/MM/YYYY and DD/MM/YY formats take precedence over MM/DD. Try (%d/%m/%Y, %d-%m-%Y, %d/%m/%y, %d-%m-%y, %d %b %Y, %d-%b-%Y, %Y-%m-%d, %Y/%m/%d) IN THAT ORDER. Reject dates that parse to the future relative to today or whose month/day is impossible; when two different dates are present, prefer the one on the line containing the token 'DATE' and co-located with a time stamp.",
      "rationale": "Fixes 034.jpg's day/month flip and generalizes to any receipt where both components are ≤12."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "Multi-Pass OCR Strategy",
      "change": "Replace the concatenation example with a 'consensus voter': run N preprocessing × PSM variants, apply extract_total and extract_date to each variant independently, and return the modal (most frequent) non-null result; break ties by preferring variants whose average per-word confidence from image_to_data is highest.",
      "rationale": "Mitigates single-digit OCR corruption like 102.00 → 702.00 on 074.jpg; generalizes to all glyph-confusion failures."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "NEW subsection: Cross-Field Numeric Sanity Check",
      "change": "Add guidance that after extracting a candidate total, scan the OCR text for other amounts that appear on lines containing SUBTOTAL, CASH, PAYMENT, TOTAL ROUNDED, or 'Cash Received - Change'. If the candidate disagrees with ≥2 of these redundant values that mutually agree, replace the candidate with the modal redundant value. Include a short worked example (safety-pins receipt: payment/subtotal/rounded all agree at 102.00; candidate 702.00 is overridden).",
      "rationale": "Directly repairs 074.jpg and gives generic robustness against single-digit OCR errors on well-structured receipts."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "NEW subsection: Tabular-Layout Recovery via image_to_data",
      "change": "Recommend grouping pytesseract.image_to_data tokens by (block_num, par_num, line_num) and extracting the right-most numeric token on any line whose leftmost tokens match a priority keyword. Provide a small snippet. State that this is the preferred fallback whenever the string-based line scanner returns None on a keyword-rich receipt.",
      "rationale": "Addresses 078.jpg (and future tabular layouts) where the label and amount are same-row but visually far apart; prevents silent empty extractions."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "Structured Field Extraction — Per-Image Pipeline with Null-Safe Failure",
      "change": "Explicitly state the extractor MUST return Python None (never '', 'None', 'nan', 0, or 0.0) on failure, and MUST NOT swallow partial successes (e.g., returning '23.' because the decimal portion was cut). Add a validation regex `^\\d+\\.\\d{2}$` applied to every returned total string, with None as the fallback on mismatch.",
      "rationale": "Prevents the 078.jpg empty-string writer drift and any similar partial-amount leakage."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "xlsx",
      "section": "Strict-Schema Outputs — Canonical Pattern",
      "change": "Insert a mandatory normalize_row() step before DataFrame construction that maps any of {'', 'None', 'none', 'nan', 'NaN', float('nan'), pd.NA} to None for every cell, and that re-formats numeric-looking totals through f'{float(x):.2f}' only when the value already matches the two-decimal regex. Show the normalize step in the code example, not as an afterthought.",
      "rationale": "Guarantees nulls are real nulls (fixes 078.jpg write-side bug) and prevents accidental float coercion of already-correct strings."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "xlsx",
      "section": "Strict-Schema Outputs — Verification",
      "change": "Expand the self-check to open the file with openpyxl (not pandas) and assert: wb.sheetnames == ['results']; header row equals the expected tuple; for each non-null cell in string-typed columns cell.data_type == 's'; no cell equals '' or 'nan'; row count equals input count; filenames are lexicographically sorted. Fail loudly if any assertion trips so the agent re-attempts before its iteration budget expires.",
      "rationale": "Catches writer-side strict-schema drift (empty strings, wrong dtype, wrong sheet name) that currently flips binary reward to 0 despite high field accuracy."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "xlsx",
      "section": "NEW subsection: Terminal Self-Check (required before claiming done)",
      "change": "Add a short checklist and code snippet to be run as the final step of any pipeline that produces a graded Excel: re-open, verify schema, verify ordering, verify null representation, verify string-amount two-decimal regex on all non-null totals; only then emit the finish signal. Note that this check must run even when the agent is near its iteration budget.",
      "rationale": "Mitigates RC6 (max_iterations termination without self-verification); the same pattern applies to any strict-schema task, not just OCR."
    },
    {
      "target_skill": "image-ocr",
      "section": "Quality Self-Check",
      "change": "Add checks: 'Chosen total line is the LAST matching line within its tier'; 'Candidate total agrees with ≥1 redundant field (subtotal/payment/rounded/cash-change) when such fields are present'; 'Date is DD/MM-first and not in the future'; 'All failures surface as Python None, never empty string'.",
      "rationale": "Formalizes the new invariants so they are testable during the agent's own review loop."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 0.82
}
